Third-party code in libterae
============================

libterae is offered under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or
later (COPYING), and under a commercial licence (LICENSING). The code listed
here comes from other projects. Each licence allows it to ship under both.

src/port/{architecture}/ holds memcpy, memmove, memset and memcmp in
assembly, for builds without a C library. The compiler calls these
functions even in freestanding code. The files taken from other projects
are kept unchanged. Each folder's NOTICE gives every such file's project,
path, commit, URL, sha256 and licence, with the full licence text where the
file doesn't carry it. These notices must go with any binary built from
those files.

