Arm Optimized Routines is offered under MIT OR Apache-2.0 WITH
LLVM-exception. libterae takes it under MIT.

src/port/generic/ is libterae's own: C memcpy, memmove, memset and memcmp,
for the folders that have no assembly for some of them, and for any
processor that has no folder, through PORT=generic. So are each
folder's port_* wrappers and the headers that stand in for other projects'.

When libterae is built with TLS, platform/ links Mbed TLS statically. Mbed
TLS is taken under the Apache License 2.0. A binary built with it must carry
that licence's text and Mbed TLS's notices, which come with its source.
